+## [3.15.0] - 2026-05-19
+
 ### Added
-- **`pd roadmap pop` — atomic claim from the curated pile** (proposed **3.15.0**, minor: new workflow surface + new durable API + new SQL table). Pops one entry from the roadmap pile (live feedback → next-cut → ideas-now → dogfood feedback by default, override with `--kind`), writes a `roadmap_claims` row, and returns the entry. Atomicity is enforced by a partial UNIQUE index `ON roadmap_claims(slug) WHERE released_at IS NULL` — two racers, one INSERT wins, the loser gets `SQLITE_CONSTRAINT` and the daemon picks the next candidate. Companion verbs: `pd roadmap release <slug>` lifts the claim; `pd roadmap claims [--mine]` shows the active claim map. Optional `--begin` flag chains into `pd begin` so a session opens with the claim's slug + summary as purpose. New routes: `POST /cartographer/roadmap-pop`, `POST /cartographer/roadmap-release`, `GET /cartographer/roadmap-claims`. Rationale + alternatives in [ADR-0033](docs/adr/0033-roadmap-pop-atomic-claim.md).
-- **Roadmap claims now link to sessions + agents** (rolls into proposed **3.15.0**, ADR-0034). `roadmap_claims` grew nullable `session_id` and `agent_id` columns plus an idempotent `ALTER TABLE` migration. `pd roadmap pop --begin` now writes the new session/agent IDs back onto the claim row, so `pd roadmap claims` surfaces "session: <id>" and a future `pd whois <slug>` can resolve cleanly. New route `POST /cartographer/roadmap-claim-link` exposes the rebind operation (idempotent; refuses to overwrite an existing link without `force: true`). New CLI verb `pd roadmap claim-link <slug> [--session <id>] [--agent <id>] [--force]` for manually attaching or rebinding a session to a claim after the fact. Schema migration is safe for existing claims (legacy rows have NULL session/agent and stay valid). Rationale in [ADR-0034](docs/adr/0034-roadmap-claim-session-link.md).
+- **Signed binary daemon distribution path** (PR #55, ADR-0028). Port Daddy now ships as `bun build --compile` single-binary daemon + CLI + MCP. New `scripts/build-daemon-binary.mjs` + `scripts/build-single-binary.mjs` produce the unsigned Mach-O; `scripts/sign-and-notarize.mjs` is the wrapper that codesigns with the Curiositech LLC Developer ID, embeds the hardened-runtime entitlements (`scripts/entitlements/port-daddy.plist`, including JIT for bun:sqlite), and submits to Apple notarytool. Three launch modes resolved by `shared/daemon-binary.ts:resolveDaemonLaunchCommand`: `binary` (the shipped, signed daemon), `source` (`PORT_DADDY_ALLOW_SOURCE_DAEMON=1` opt-in for dev), `self` (single-binary self-host via `PORT_DADDY_CAN_SELF_DAEMON=1`). Unconventional bun-virtual-fs layouts now fall back to `dirname(execPath)` with a one-shot warning instead of silently using `process.cwd()`. Existing v3.14.x users running tsx server.ts are unaffected; `pd install` regenerates the LaunchAgent against the new binary.
+- **`pd doctor` resilience checks 12 + 13** (PR #77, into PR #55). Check 12 — **LaunchAgent target**: reads `~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.portdaddy.daemon.plist`, normalizes binary plists via `plutil -convert xml1` before string-matching, and fails with the hint `Run: port-daddy install` when the plist still targets the legacy `tsx server.ts` launcher (the silent-upgrade trap where `brew upgrade` appears to do nothing because launchd keeps spawning the old path). Regex is scoped to path-shaped `<string>` values so prose mentioning `server.ts` in `<key>Comment</key>` doesn't false-positive. Check 13 — **Resource directory**: prints a four-line breakdown of `PORT_DADDY_RESOURCE_DIR` resolution (env override / module dir / bun-virtual-fs flag / resolved root / expected binary path with presence). Replaces the regression guard formerly at `scripts/promote-stable.sh:144-148`, now reachable for every user.
+- **bun:sqlite pragma routing — extracted `executeBunPragma` helper** (PR #55). Pure function (`execSql, querySql, stmt, opts`) routing the three better-sqlite3 `.pragma()` call shapes (setter `journal_mode = WAL`, function `wal_checkpoint(TRUNCATE)`, getter `journal_mode` with optional `{ simple: true }`) onto bun:sqlite's `exec` + `query.all` primitives. 9 unit tests cover routing + a column-name-divergence path (`Object.values(rows[0])[0]` extraction survives whatever key bun:sqlite returns).
+- **Pull Request Operating Procedure** in `AGENTS.md` (PR #83). Seven-step doctrine: open PR with `pd begin` + file claims → spawn `feature-dev:code-reviewer` agent demanding `SHIP / SHIP-AFTER-FIX / DO-NOT-SHIP` verdict → fixup commit per HIGH-confidence finding → PR comment with validation evidence → re-spawn reviewer for non-trivial change sets → `pd note` + `pd done` → merge in dependency order with stacked-PR rebase.
+- **`pd roadmap pop` — atomic claim from the curated pile** (PR #91, ADR-0033). Pops one entry from the roadmap pile (live feedback → next-cut → ideas-now → dogfood feedback by default, override with `--kind`), writes a `roadmap_claims` row, returns the entry. Atomicity enforced by a partial UNIQUE index `ON roadmap_claims(slug) WHERE released_at IS NULL` — two racers, one INSERT wins, the loser gets `SQLITE_CONSTRAINT` and the daemon picks the next candidate. Companion verbs: `pd roadmap release <slug>` lifts the claim; `pd roadmap claims [--mine]` shows the active claim map. Optional `--begin` flag chains into `pd begin` so a session opens with the claim's slug + summary as purpose. New routes: `POST /cartographer/roadmap-pop`, `POST /cartographer/roadmap-release`, `GET /cartographer/roadmap-claims`.
+- **Roadmap claims now link to sessions + agents** (ADR-0034). `roadmap_claims` grew nullable `session_id` and `agent_id` columns plus an idempotent `ALTER TABLE` migration. `pd roadmap pop --begin` now writes the new session/agent IDs back onto the claim row, so `pd roadmap claims` surfaces "session: <id>" and a future `pd whois <slug>` can resolve cleanly. New route `POST /cartographer/roadmap-claim-link` exposes the rebind operation (idempotent; refuses to overwrite an existing link without `force: true`). New CLI verb `pd roadmap claim-link <slug> [--session <id>] [--agent <id>] [--force]` for manually attaching or rebinding a session to a claim after the fact. Schema migration is safe for existing claims (legacy rows have NULL session/agent and stay valid). Rationale in [ADR-0034](docs/adr/0034-roadmap-claim-session-link.md).
+
+### Fixed
+
+- **Cross-project claim leak on destructive git verbs** (PR #74). PD's `session_files` (claims) table is host-global across all repos. The pre-rebase/cherry-pick/reset/stash-push guard called `loadAllActiveClaims()` and treated every claim as if it belonged to the current repo — a marketing agent in some other repo claiming `apps/marketing/src/app/page.tsx` could block an unrelated port-daddy rebase. Added `filterClaimsToRepo(paths, repoRoot)` which canonicalizes both the repo root and each candidate path via `realpathSync` before the containment check (catches symlink escapes outside the repo and macOS `/var` → `/private/var` traversal). Subsumes the old `existsSync` gate — `realpathSync` throwing covers broken symlinks, missing files, and unresolvable paths uniformly. 11 new regression tests.
+- **`tests/unit/blob.test.js` macOS-24 timing flake** (PR #55). GC test ran with a 20ms sleep + 10ms `olderThanMs` threshold; on macOS-latest node-24 the gap between `store.put(fresh)` and `store.gc()` occasionally exceeded 10ms under runner load and reaped fresh, failing the "too new to reap" assertion. Bumped to 100ms sleep + 50ms threshold — wide margin both sides, still under 250ms.
+- **`/tmp` hardcode in `scripts/build-single-binary.mjs`** (PR #55). The self-hosted-daemon smoke prefix was `join('/tmp', ...)` despite `tmpdir` from `node:os` being imported and correctly used 70 lines below. Replaced with `tmpdir()` — macOS purges /tmp on reboot, and the project's standing ban makes any /tmp write a defect.
+
+### Changed
+- **`AGENTS.md` operator workflow surface** picks up the new PR operating procedure (PR #83) and continues to point users at `pd briefing` / `pd salvage` / `pd begin` as the on-ramp for any non-trivial repo edit.
 
